# The .gitignore created by Unreal Engine exludes some files and directories.
# A different approach is to exclude everything except what we need.

# The following gitignore settings were mostly written by the github account MOZGII,
# they were slightly modified by Maven Dev to account for the .gitignore being a dir
# level higher than the Unreal Engine project dir. Plugin specificity was also added.

# Ignore all files by default, but scan all directories.
*
!*/

# Do not ignore git files in the root of the repo.
!/.git*

# Do not ignore the read me file.
!README.md

# Do not ignore current project's `.uproject`.
!*/*.uproject

# Do not ignore the steam_appid if the project has one
!*/*steam_appid.txt

# Do not ignore source and config dirs.
!*/Source/**
!*/Config/**

# Plugin dirs are a project in of themselves, so they get extra specificity.
!*/Plugins/*/*.uplugin
!*/Plugins/*/Config/**
!*/Plugins/*/Source/**
!*/Plugins/*/Resources/**

# Only allow .uasset and .umap files from /Content dir.
# They're tracked by git-lfs, don't forget to track other
# files if adding them here.
!*/Content/**/*.uasset
!*/Content/**/*.umap

# Allow any files from /NonEngineContent dir.
# Any file in /NonEngineContent dir will be managed by git lfs.
# This is where art assets (like .fbx) would be stored.
!/NonEngineContent/**/*
